-- title:
--   Edge structure constants force nilpotent coordinates modulo [p]
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a commutative Noetherian ring $R$ of characteristic $p$, together with a ring homomorphism $j\colon W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2}) \to R$ from the Witt vectors of the field `GaloisField p 2` (written `Zp2 p`), and elements $\xi,\eta \in R$ with $\xi\eta = 0$. Let $X$ be a `FormalODModule p R`: a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $R$ equipped with an action `act` of `Zp2 p` by endomorphisms of $F$ (unital, multiplicative under composition, additive via $F$) and an endomorphism `varpi` of $F$ satisfying $\varpi \circ \varpi = \mathrm{act}(p)$ and $\varpi \circ \mathrm{act}(a) = \mathrm{act}(\sigma a) \circ \varpi$ for the Witt–Frobenius $\sigma$. Let $\gamma_0,\gamma_1$ be elements of the Cartier module of $F$ forming a homogeneous $V$-basis relative to $j$: each $\gamma_i$ lies in the graded piece of index $i$, i.e. the Teichmüller element $\tau(c)$, $c \in \mathbb{F}_{p^2}$, acts on $\gamma_i$ as the homothety by $j(\tau(c))^{p^i}$, and the matrix of tangent coefficients of the $\gamma_i$ has unit determinant. Assume $\gamma$ has structure constants `EdgeFamily.edgeConstants p ξ η` for the action of $\varpi$: for every $i$ and every $N$ there is an element $h$ of the Cartier module with $\varpi_*\gamma_i = \sum_{m<N} V^m\bigl(a_{m,i}\cdot \gamma_{(m+i+1) \bmod 2}\bigr) + V^N h$, where $a_{m,0}$ (resp. $a_{m,1}$) is the branch constant of $\eta$ (resp. of $\xi$) at $m$, namely $x^p - x$ for $m=0$, $1$ for $m=1$, the $(m/2)$-th Witt digit of $x$ raised to the $p^{m/2}$ for even $m \geq 2$, and $0$ for odd $m \geq 3$. The conclusion is that there exists $N \in \mathbb{N}$ such that for each $i \in \{0,1\}$ the monomial $X_i^N$ lies in the ideal of $R[[X_0,X_1]]$ generated by the two components of $\mathrm{act}(p)$, the power series giving multiplication by $p$ on $X$.
--
--   The assertion is that the kernel of multiplication by $p$ on such a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module is infinitesimal of finite order, the coordinate functions being nilpotent modulo the ideal generated by $[p]$; over a Noetherian base this is what makes the kernel algebras finite and stable under base change. It is used in establishing that the edge-constant formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules have height four, both over perfect rings and over algebraically closed fields.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_exists_X_pow_mem_span_act_of_hasStructureConstants_edgeConstants.lean

